{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And when a soul brings a meal-offering</b> — 'soul' is said regarding a meal-offering because it comes with his soul, for the poor person exerts himself until he obtains [enough] to bring it. Regarding bird-offerings and meal-offerings, 'before YHWH' is not said, as it is regarding cattle, because poor people bring them and are ashamed to bring them before everyone. Therefore He said to Aaron and to his sons, who are not in public, and He warned Aaron alone, that even the High Priest must not despise the meal-offering of the poor."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:57.341602573Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}